WEBVTT

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.751
Made it!

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.192
Huh?

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.163
Hello?

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.996
Hello?! Are you alive?!

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:39.037
Gramps! There's a girl!
A girl's collapsed down there!

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:49.149
You know the continuation of
the fairy tale I've wanted to hear about?

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:55.713
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:07.233
It's like we were both seeking
a coincidence that was off by a page

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.402
And that's how
fate brought us together

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:17.577
More than those words
that you once kept to yourself

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:26.486
It's the kindness
that made you keep them to yourself

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:33.493
That I want to have faith in now

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:41.201
You know, we'll be living
alongside uncertainty from now on

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:47.607
We used to have nothing to lose,
but that's not us now

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:55.315
You know the continuation of
the fairy tale I didn't know about before?

00:01:55.315 --> 00:02:01.588
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:05.547
It's something to build up bit by bit

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.870
"Where She Found Herself"
All right, I've finished processing you.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.971
"Where She Found Herself"
Good luck.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.836
"Where She Found Herself"
Thanks.

00:02:28.311 --> 00:02:29.746
Yuto.

00:02:29.746 --> 00:02:32.081
Have you found any information on Solty?

00:02:32.081 --> 00:02:34.317
Nothing yet.

00:02:34.317 --> 00:02:36.820
The surveillance camera checks
came up empty, too.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.888
I see.

00:02:38.888 --> 00:02:41.658
I'll expand my
search parameters a bit more.

00:02:41.658 --> 00:02:43.159
Please do that.

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:45.094
I know you must be tired
from staying up all night...

00:02:45.094 --> 00:02:46.891
No, not at all.

00:02:48.431 --> 00:02:51.401
Kasha, isn't it almost time for school?

00:02:51.401 --> 00:02:54.768
Yeah. I'm gonna go.

00:02:59.108 --> 00:03:02.145
Say, want me to walk you to school?

00:03:02.145 --> 00:03:04.047
There's something I want to go buy anyway,

00:03:04.047 --> 00:03:05.815
so I thought we could, you know...

00:03:05.815 --> 00:03:08.318
Don't treat me like a child!

00:03:08.318 --> 00:03:12.277
Never mind me!
You make sure you find Solty!

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:21.058
Even Kasha's being so strong, but Roy...

00:03:33.743 --> 00:03:35.677
I'm hungry.

00:03:52.095 --> 00:03:56.232
Rita's dead! What am I?!

00:03:56.232 --> 00:03:59.167
Why am I so?!

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.508
Where am I?

00:04:20.223 --> 00:04:22.692
Mr. Roy, please wait!

00:04:22.692 --> 00:04:25.762
Please do not go, Mr. Roy!

00:04:25.762 --> 00:04:29.465
Why?! Is it because I am a machine?!

00:04:29.465 --> 00:04:31.933
If I were human would you...

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:34.568
Mr. Roy!

00:04:40.043 --> 00:04:41.772
So you're awake.

00:04:43.546 --> 00:04:46.215
You seem to have
strained yourself quite a bit.

00:04:46.215 --> 00:04:48.918
Various components throughout
your body were being overloaded.

00:04:48.918 --> 00:04:52.388
The Al overflow was
particularly troublesome.

00:04:52.388 --> 00:04:54.913
But it's a good thing
I had some spare parts.

00:04:57.794 --> 00:04:59.362
Um...

00:04:59.362 --> 00:05:01.531
Won't you tell me a little about it?

00:05:01.531 --> 00:05:03.166
What?

00:05:03.166 --> 00:05:05.327
About what you've been through.

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:12.402
What were you doing in a place like this?

00:05:14.644 --> 00:05:17.146
When did you arrive?

00:05:17.146 --> 00:05:19.749
What is your purpose?

00:05:19.749 --> 00:05:21.851
Can't you hear me?

00:05:21.851 --> 00:05:24.053
Could it be the language circuits
are damaged?

00:05:24.053 --> 00:05:25.254
No, they are not!

00:05:25.254 --> 00:05:27.950
Please do not talk about me like that.

00:05:29.759 --> 00:05:33.696
Does anyone know you're here?

00:05:33.696 --> 00:05:35.186
Answer me.

00:05:36.766 --> 00:05:39.702
I do not wish to answer that.

00:05:39.702 --> 00:05:41.771
I never thought it possible, but...

00:05:41.771 --> 00:05:44.741
Are you self-aware?

00:05:44.741 --> 00:05:46.309
Um...

00:05:46.309 --> 00:05:52.548
I will not make any trouble,
so would you mind putting that gun down?

00:05:52.548 --> 00:05:53.549
Oh...

00:05:53.549 --> 00:05:58.488
It is dangerous. If a bullet ricochets,
it could hit you.

00:05:58.488 --> 00:06:00.513
You have a point.

00:06:02.658 --> 00:06:04.327
I appreciate your help.

00:06:04.327 --> 00:06:07.854
Thank you for saving me.

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:27.350
Hey!

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:28.584
Oh...

00:06:28.584 --> 00:06:31.287
I'm glad to see you
regained consciousness!

00:06:31.287 --> 00:06:34.157
I was shocked when I first found you.

00:06:34.157 --> 00:06:35.858
You were unconscious
in the middle of nowhere!

00:06:35.858 --> 00:06:37.760
I thought it might've been my fault!

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.063
Oh, I'm Will. Nice to meet you.

00:06:40.063 --> 00:06:42.198
Huh? Oh...

00:06:42.198 --> 00:06:44.400
Pleased to meet you.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.368
What's your name?

00:06:45.368 --> 00:06:46.969
Oh, right.

00:06:46.969 --> 00:06:48.571
It is Solty.

00:06:48.571 --> 00:06:50.406
Solty, huh?

00:06:50.406 --> 00:06:53.643
Say, why were you unconscious
in a place like that?

00:06:53.643 --> 00:06:54.377
What?

00:06:54.377 --> 00:06:57.113
Were you on a solo journey?

00:06:57.113 --> 00:06:59.248
- Oh... No, I was...
- Talk about dangerous!
You need to be careful!

00:06:59.248 --> 00:07:00.416
Oh, this?

00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:03.686
These are parts for the plane I'm building.

00:07:03.686 --> 00:07:04.420
What?

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.621
Want to have a look?

00:07:05.621 --> 00:07:07.589
Huh? Um...

00:07:16.499 --> 00:07:18.334
This is a plane?

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:20.303
Yup! Never seen one before?

00:07:20.303 --> 00:07:21.471
Oh, no.

00:07:21.471 --> 00:07:23.272
Isn't it awesome?!

00:07:23.272 --> 00:07:25.842
This is a machine to go
flying in the sky with!

00:07:25.842 --> 00:07:26.809
In the sky?

00:07:26.809 --> 00:07:29.545
Like this... Zoom!

00:07:29.545 --> 00:07:33.616
Of course, it can't go so high
as to get caught in the altitude limit.

00:07:33.616 --> 00:07:35.384
Not that I even want to.

00:07:35.384 --> 00:07:39.055
But man, it wasn't easy
getting it built to this point!

00:07:39.055 --> 00:07:41.424
It's not like they sell parts
for this kind of thing, after all.

00:07:41.424 --> 00:07:44.727
For every part I needed, I'd go
all the way to the city to scrounge for it

00:07:44.727 --> 00:07:45.928
and that's how I put this together.

00:07:45.928 --> 00:07:47.263
Scrounging?

00:07:47.263 --> 00:07:48.364
Yeah!

00:07:48.364 --> 00:07:52.735
All the parts for this come from things
that were thrown away in the city.

00:07:52.735 --> 00:07:54.794
You might say I recycle discarded items.

00:08:00.643 --> 00:08:03.079
Things that were thrown away...

00:08:03.079 --> 00:08:06.115
Well, it's like I was "thrown away" myself

00:08:06.115 --> 00:08:08.918
and Gramps is someone
who "threw away" the life he had,

00:08:08.918 --> 00:08:10.753
so it seems pretty fitting.

00:08:10.753 --> 00:08:13.422
Hm, maybe I've said a little too much.

00:08:13.422 --> 00:08:14.891
Then...

00:08:14.891 --> 00:08:15.958
Huh?

00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:21.531
...maybe someday you can use me
as parts for this, as well.

00:08:21.531 --> 00:08:22.865
What? Can I, really?!

00:08:22.865 --> 00:08:24.033
What?

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:25.398
Uh...

00:08:30.373 --> 00:08:32.241
Awesome! Just awesome!

00:08:32.241 --> 00:08:34.076
You're really strong!

00:08:34.076 --> 00:08:37.443
Um, this is not what I meant
when I said you could use me!

00:08:43.553 --> 00:08:46.920
Okay! Now, I'll just get it stabilized and...

00:08:49.959 --> 00:08:51.051
Mr. Will!

00:08:54.764 --> 00:08:56.365
Mr. Will!

00:08:56.365 --> 00:08:57.733
Mr. Will...

00:08:57.733 --> 00:08:59.701
Mr. Will!

00:09:00.836 --> 00:09:03.031
No, he cannot be...

00:09:06.909 --> 00:09:09.145
Did I scare you?

00:09:09.145 --> 00:09:11.080
It was a joke! Just a joke!

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.416
A bit of mischief, if you will.

00:09:13.416 --> 00:09:16.586
Well, laugh it off and forgive me, okay?

00:09:16.586 --> 00:09:18.144
Wait, what?

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.124
What?!

00:09:22.124 --> 00:09:24.126
Uh, er, um, l-I'm sorry!

00:09:24.126 --> 00:09:25.695
I-I never meant it that way!

00:09:25.695 --> 00:09:28.562
Hold on! Why... Huh?

00:09:38.574 --> 00:09:39.609
Man...

00:09:39.609 --> 00:09:43.613
She was crying one minute
and then she suddenly collapsed!

00:09:43.613 --> 00:09:46.649
Oh, I didn't do anything to her!
Really, I didn't!

00:09:46.649 --> 00:09:48.784
No one's saying you did.

00:09:48.784 --> 00:09:52.083
But who the heck is this girl anyway?

00:09:53.422 --> 00:09:55.788
You know, don't you, Gramps?

00:10:00.162 --> 00:10:03.466
Respiration and pulse are stable
and within acceptable parameters.

00:10:03.466 --> 00:10:05.501
Brain wave level: Green.

00:10:05.501 --> 00:10:08.871
Readings complete for lines 72 through 88.

00:10:08.871 --> 00:10:11.207
Recording a control coefficient of 0.65.

00:10:11.207 --> 00:10:13.437
Processing speed still increasing.

00:10:15.878 --> 00:10:19.215
She's connecting the
operational lines herself!

00:10:19.215 --> 00:10:21.284
Tension coefficient is virtually negligible!

00:10:21.284 --> 00:10:24.320
She's feeling no
control stress at all, either!

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.589
She is incredibly gifted!

00:10:26.589 --> 00:10:29.251
Why have you kept her from us until now?

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.135
Huh?

00:10:39.135 --> 00:10:41.904
- Accela?
- Oh, Silvia.

00:10:41.904 --> 00:10:45.241
Wasn't today your day on that program?

00:10:45.241 --> 00:10:47.243
It was cancelled for today.

00:10:47.243 --> 00:10:48.744
I see.

00:10:48.744 --> 00:10:54.050
Are you working with Integra and
the others on that incident, Sylvia?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:56.152
Yeah.

00:10:56.152 --> 00:10:59.322
You guys had to handle everything
while I was hospitalized,

00:10:59.322 --> 00:11:01.757
so I figure I'd better do
some work to return the favor.

00:11:01.757 --> 00:11:03.793
Not at all! Oh...

00:11:03.793 --> 00:11:05.461
Huh?

00:11:05.461 --> 00:11:07.663
Silvia, your makeup...

00:11:07.663 --> 00:11:12.702
Oh, Celica insisted on
putting this on just earlier...

00:11:12.702 --> 00:11:13.836
It looks terrific.

00:11:13.836 --> 00:11:16.672
But never mind that,
what's happened to you today?

00:11:16.672 --> 00:11:17.673
Huh?

00:11:17.673 --> 00:11:20.476
You're so talkative.

00:11:20.476 --> 00:11:22.078
R-Really?

00:11:22.078 --> 00:11:24.246
It's unusual for you.

00:11:24.246 --> 00:11:25.548
Is it odd?

00:11:25.548 --> 00:11:28.451
No, it's a good trend.

00:11:28.451 --> 00:11:30.078
Sorry for bothering you.

00:12:05.421 --> 00:12:07.623
Now, don't hold back! Dig in!

00:12:07.623 --> 00:12:11.260
It's been a while since
I've worked this hard on dinner!

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.196
I told you never to cook!

00:12:14.196 --> 00:12:16.866
I wish you wouldn't judge
the food by its appearance!

00:12:16.866 --> 00:12:19.702
It's the taste! What counts is the taste!

00:12:19.702 --> 00:12:23.539
You should've just quietly
served the usual packaged foods.

00:12:23.539 --> 00:12:27.276
That wouldn't show
our sincerity to our guest.

00:12:27.276 --> 00:12:28.944
Don't worry!

00:12:28.944 --> 00:12:31.071
One bite and you'll...

00:12:38.687 --> 00:12:41.490
That's why I've told you
not to let me cook!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.825
You never learn!

00:12:42.825 --> 00:12:43.959
Oh, um...

00:12:43.959 --> 00:12:44.860
Huh?

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.530
Shall I recook dinner?

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.690
Really?

00:12:56.338 --> 00:12:57.862
Wow!

00:12:59.175 --> 00:13:01.944
Th-This is how it turned out...

00:13:01.944 --> 00:13:03.775
Thanks for the food!

00:13:05.281 --> 00:13:07.483
H-How is it?

00:13:07.483 --> 00:13:09.351
Delicious! It's delicious!

00:13:09.351 --> 00:13:12.655
I am glad!

00:13:12.655 --> 00:13:16.358
You know, if you don't have
any place to go, just stay with us!

00:13:16.358 --> 00:13:20.329
And you can cook for us like this!
How about it?

00:13:20.329 --> 00:13:21.363
Hey!

00:13:21.363 --> 00:13:22.097
What?!

00:13:22.097 --> 00:13:22.932
You idiot!

00:13:22.932 --> 00:13:23.866
What'd you call me that for?!

00:13:23.866 --> 00:13:25.401
Use your head a little!

00:13:25.401 --> 00:13:26.869
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:13:26.869 --> 00:13:28.871
You're not making any sense!

00:13:28.871 --> 00:13:31.271
Hey, are you ignoring me?!

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.515
Thanks!

00:13:39.515 --> 00:13:41.484
Now, bring that over here.

00:13:41.484 --> 00:13:42.451
Sure.

00:13:44.487 --> 00:13:46.856
Okay! Slowly, now.

00:13:46.856 --> 00:13:47.880
Right.

00:13:56.332 --> 00:13:58.734
For a while there, I wasn't sure
what would happened,

00:13:58.734 --> 00:14:01.537
but I'm glad it's back to the way it was.

00:14:01.537 --> 00:14:03.706
Thank you for helping me!

00:14:03.706 --> 00:14:06.108
Oh, it was nothing.

00:14:06.108 --> 00:14:07.543
You don't smile, do you?

00:14:07.543 --> 00:14:08.544
Huh?

00:14:08.544 --> 00:14:11.347
You haven't smiled once since yesterday.

00:14:11.347 --> 00:14:13.716
Could it be because you can't?

00:14:13.716 --> 00:14:14.917
No, nothing like that.

00:14:14.917 --> 00:14:16.919
That's no smile.

00:14:16.919 --> 00:14:18.621
What?

00:14:18.621 --> 00:14:21.824
It'd make me happy if you told me...

00:14:21.824 --> 00:14:24.793
...the real reason why you
can't smile wholeheartedly.

00:14:29.465 --> 00:14:31.367
I see...

00:14:31.367 --> 00:14:32.959
Now, I understand.

00:14:35.237 --> 00:14:37.873
You hate your mechanical body that much?

00:14:37.873 --> 00:14:39.475
I hate it.

00:14:39.475 --> 00:14:44.914
But because of it you were able
to save your stepfather, right?

00:14:44.914 --> 00:14:46.115
But...

00:14:46.115 --> 00:14:48.379
What could a mechanical puppet
like you understand?!

00:14:55.357 --> 00:14:59.595
As for me, I envy your mechanical body.

00:14:59.595 --> 00:15:00.721
What?

00:15:03.132 --> 00:15:06.001
Human beings inevitably die, right?

00:15:06.001 --> 00:15:08.837
From injury, illness,
or maybe it's just their time.

00:15:08.837 --> 00:15:11.907
With a mechanical body,
you could live forever.

00:15:11.907 --> 00:15:14.843
Is that a good thing?

00:15:14.843 --> 00:15:16.145
Who knows?

00:15:16.145 --> 00:15:18.013
Beats me!

00:15:18.013 --> 00:15:22.551
People always envy what others have.

00:15:22.551 --> 00:15:25.921
Maybe that's why I envy
your mechanical body.

00:15:25.921 --> 00:15:27.445
The opposite is also true.

00:15:28.857 --> 00:15:31.060
If it causes you so much grief,

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.862
you should throw it all away,
once and for all.

00:15:33.862 --> 00:15:34.830
Huh?

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:39.168
Your body, your stepfather, everything...

00:15:39.168 --> 00:15:41.770
This is a place where you can do that.

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.773
I think it'll make you feel
a whole lot better.

00:15:44.773 --> 00:15:46.842
I do not think...

00:15:46.842 --> 00:15:48.544
...I could...

00:15:48.544 --> 00:15:51.480
Whether it's family or friends...

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.983
Love or life...

00:15:53.983 --> 00:15:57.319
You can throw away
whatever you have at any time.

00:15:57.319 --> 00:16:00.652
And I mean, at any time.
The instant you decide to do it.

00:16:02.725 --> 00:16:03.885
But...

00:16:06.629 --> 00:16:08.731
But if you have any lingering attachments,

00:16:08.731 --> 00:16:11.100
why not try clinging to them for now?

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:13.936
No matter how shameless it may seem.

00:16:13.936 --> 00:16:16.205
You can always throw them away later.

00:16:16.205 --> 00:16:18.607
At any time.

00:16:18.607 --> 00:16:21.677
As for me, I'd like you
to stay here if possible.

00:16:21.677 --> 00:16:22.911
What?

00:16:22.911 --> 00:16:24.913
Can't you tell?

00:16:24.913 --> 00:16:26.548
That I'm in love with you!

00:16:26.548 --> 00:16:27.606
Huh?!

00:16:33.155 --> 00:16:37.660
Uh, um, no one has ever said
something like that to me before,

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.496
so I do not know how to respond. Um...

00:16:40.496 --> 00:16:42.631
Gotcha!

00:16:42.631 --> 00:16:44.066
Surprised?

00:16:44.066 --> 00:16:45.167
What?

00:16:45.167 --> 00:16:46.702
Up we go.

00:16:46.702 --> 00:16:48.771
It was a joke! Just a joke!

00:16:48.771 --> 00:16:50.806
A bit of mischief, if you will.

00:16:50.806 --> 00:16:54.109
Look, it's almost dinner time.

00:16:54.109 --> 00:16:56.245
Would you cook us something
delicious again tonight?

00:16:56.245 --> 00:16:59.114
What? Oh, certainly!

00:16:59.114 --> 00:17:00.775
Then I'll be counting on you!

00:17:16.432 --> 00:17:19.367
Darn it. I don't have much time left.

00:17:22.271 --> 00:17:23.439
Miranda!

00:17:23.439 --> 00:17:24.599
Huh?

00:17:40.856 --> 00:17:43.992
We might be able to track down Solty.

00:17:43.992 --> 00:17:46.187
We got information
from someone who saw her.

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.265
So, you have no response to that...

00:17:50.265 --> 00:17:52.868
What would you have me do?!

00:17:52.868 --> 00:17:55.671
What do you want to do?

00:17:55.671 --> 00:17:56.905
Nothing.

00:17:56.905 --> 00:17:58.874
Roy!

00:17:58.874 --> 00:18:03.378
I've lost my daughter. Twice.

00:18:03.378 --> 00:18:08.484
What is it that you want me to do?!

00:18:08.484 --> 00:18:11.420
Don't act like you're the only victim!

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.723
You're not the only one who lost family!

00:18:14.723 --> 00:18:18.887
I lost my husband, too!

00:18:20.028 --> 00:18:23.987
But I still had Kasha!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.933
You still had Solty!

00:18:30.339 --> 00:18:31.966
Mr. Roy!

00:18:37.045 --> 00:18:42.184
Don't you care that you'll lose her
if you just keep doing nothing?!

00:18:42.184 --> 00:18:43.879
That you'll lose that girl, too?!

00:18:48.457 --> 00:18:49.515
Roy...

00:18:54.863 --> 00:18:56.799
What? Me, too?

00:18:56.799 --> 00:19:00.903
Yup! So, when the plane
leaves the ground, hop in.

00:19:00.903 --> 00:19:02.004
- Okay?
- But...

00:19:02.004 --> 00:19:03.138
Okay?!

00:19:03.138 --> 00:19:04.571
Yes...

00:19:24.159 --> 00:19:25.961
Looking good!

00:19:25.961 --> 00:19:28.463
Looking good! Just a little more!

00:19:28.463 --> 00:19:29.953
Now! Hop in!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.500
Fly!

00:19:46.582 --> 00:19:49.985
Well? Isn't this view the best you've seen?

00:19:49.985 --> 00:19:52.521
Yes! It is the best!

00:19:52.521 --> 00:19:57.059
When I see things like this,
I can't help but feel

00:19:57.059 --> 00:20:00.062
that the world isn't
such a bad place after all.

00:20:00.062 --> 00:20:02.865
I agree!

00:20:02.865 --> 00:20:04.399
You finally smiled.

00:20:04.399 --> 00:20:05.234
Huh?

00:20:05.234 --> 00:20:07.236
I feel on top of the world!

00:20:07.236 --> 00:20:09.805
I don't care if I die now!

00:20:09.805 --> 00:20:11.102
What?

00:20:15.544 --> 00:20:16.545
You must not!

00:20:16.545 --> 00:20:20.382
You must never say things
like not caring about dying!

00:20:20.382 --> 00:20:22.050
Solty...

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.415
You must not!

00:20:26.221 --> 00:20:29.391
Gotcha! It was a joke! Just a joke!

00:20:29.391 --> 00:20:30.592
Mr. Will...

00:20:30.592 --> 00:20:33.862
Did I scare you? Now, will you let go of me?

00:20:33.862 --> 00:20:34.851
Oh...

00:20:36.765 --> 00:20:38.392
That was a bit embarrassing.

00:20:40.369 --> 00:20:45.340
Um, Mr. Will? About what
you said yesterday... Um, I...

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.609
Oh, sorry about yesterday.

00:20:47.609 --> 00:20:49.544
It was just a joke, really.

00:20:49.544 --> 00:20:52.814
I just felt like being
a little mean to you.

00:20:52.814 --> 00:20:53.715
What?

00:20:53.715 --> 00:20:57.586
I was feeling sort of frustrated...
Envious...

00:20:57.586 --> 00:21:02.958
So, I guess I wanted to leave my own
little mark on this world somewhere.

00:21:02.958 --> 00:21:04.092
Um, what do you...

00:21:04.092 --> 00:21:06.361
But believe me when I say this.

00:21:06.361 --> 00:21:08.330
I was half serious.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.627
Mr. Will?

00:21:31.386 --> 00:21:33.388
Mr. Will!

00:21:33.388 --> 00:21:35.090
Mr. Will!

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:38.126
Mr. Will! Mr. Will!

00:21:38.126 --> 00:21:39.559
Mr. Will!

00:21:52.504 --> 00:21:57.275
On a clear day in the park

00:21:57.275 --> 00:22:00.212
Looking up at the sky

00:22:00.212 --> 00:22:08.449
There was a tiny little cloud
that almost vanished

00:22:11.456 --> 00:22:16.228
Letting the wind take us where it will

00:22:16.228 --> 00:22:19.164
We live freely

00:22:19.164 --> 00:22:25.069
We make our way,
walking a little at a time

00:22:27.205 --> 00:22:31.977
We're the same

00:22:31.977 --> 00:22:36.748
This precious time

00:22:36.748 --> 00:22:40.585
Each time we meet

00:22:40.585 --> 00:22:50.095
This feeling of not being alone
turns into kindness

00:22:50.095 --> 00:22:56.701
I can turn it into the courage
to believe in someone

00:22:56.701 --> 00:23:08.772
And surely, before I vanish
into the far reaches of that sky...

00:23:15.587 --> 00:23:17.989
What I can do...

00:23:17.989 --> 00:23:20.125
To me, you are...

00:23:20.125 --> 00:23:20.258
Next time, "I Was Half Kidding".

00:23:20.258 --> 00:23:23.228
Next time, "I Was Half Kidding".
